  "title": "COVAR, COVARIANCE.P, and COVARIANCE.S skip non-numeric pairs, validate singletons before shape, and center via two-pass means",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, COVAR(array1, array2), COVARIANCE.P(array1, array2), and COVARIANCE.S(array1, array2) validate single-cell blank/error arguments in formula order before checking array shape (#N/A on mismatch), skip positions where either input holds text, logical, or blank, and compute sum((x - mean_x) * (y - mean_y)) / denom in binary64 from two-pass sample means: COVAR and COVARIANCE.P divide by n (returning 0 for 1 numeric pair and #DIV/0! for 0 pairs), whereas COVARIANCE.S divides by n - 1 (returning #DIV/0! when fewer than 2 numeric pairs exist). Matches 2,855/2,855 COVAR, 2,849/2,849 COVARIANCE.P, and 2,850/2,850 COVARIANCE.S full-bank rows.",
